.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH supazip 1  "supazip 1.0.1" 
.SH NAME
supazip \- A PeaZip\-style archive manager for 7z and ZIP (CLI front\-end).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsupazip\fR [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
SupaZip CLI — list, extract, create, and test 7z and ZIP archives. See https://github.com/your\-org/supazip for the GUI front\-end and core engine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: text]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: Human\-readable table (the legacy default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: JSON
.IP \(bu 2
yaml: YAML
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
supazip\-list(1)
List the contents of an archive
.TP
supazip\-extract(1)
Extract an archive to a directory
.TP
supazip\-create(1)
Create a new archive from one or more files
.TP
supazip\-test(1)
Verify the integrity of an archive
.TP
supazip\-completions(1)
Generate shell completion scripts (bash, zsh, fish, powershell, elvish)
.TP
supazip\-man(1)
Generate man page
.TP
supazip\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v1.0.1
